      "writtenOn": "2023-01-13T04:15:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do not think this is actually true. It is true of the pointer to the `byte[]`s that are written to this SparseArray, but not of the contents of these `byte[]`s.\n\nExample of one thing that doesn\u0027t work :\n■ Thread 1 is called with family \u003d INET6. mSockDiagMsg.get(family) is null, therefore it will call buildInetDiagReqForAliveTcpSockets, which returns a byte array. The pointer to that byte array is stored in the SparseArray. The next line correctly sends the message to the fd\n■ Later, Thread 2 is called with family \u003d INET6.\n　• If Thread 2 finds null in the SparseArray, then your reasoning is correct. It will simply build a new message and it\u0027s fine.\n　• But Thread 2 may find non-null in the SparseArray, and when it follows the pointer to the byte array, it sees the memory pointed to being full of 0 because there was no thread barrier (or, it may see only the start of the array). In that case, the message sent to the kernel is incorrect.",
      "parentUuid": "611e3312_06f0322c",
