      "side": 1,
      "message": "Again, in what sense does this method receive \"the request message\" \"from kernel\" ? It will receive any message at all from anybody at all won\u0027t it ?\n\nWe should straighten the contract for this method. The method name should reflect exactly what the method *does*, and the documentation should agree.\n\nIn this case it seems you have constraints on what the fd should be. That should be reflected in the name of the argument and in the documentation, and possibly in the name of the method if it\u0027s important enough. Then, this method is using a specific buffer size and a specific timeout. There has to be a reason for this. The reason should be documented (not the specific values, that doesn\u0027t matter – what matters is *what* this does, and *why* it does it like this).",
